      "message": "fix(post): state G17 and G94 in the Fanuc and Doosan DNM preambles\n\nA FANUC control can keep G18 / G19 or G95 from an earlier program, MDI\nor its power-on parameters. The Fanuc section preamble stated neither\nthe plane nor the feed mode, and the Doosan DNM preamble did not state\nthe feed mode. Then XY arcs, cutter compensation and drilling cycles\ncan run in the wrong plane, and an mm/min F word is read as mm/rev.\n\nBoth preambles now write G90 G17 G94 <wcs> G40 G49 G80. The Fanuc post\nalso sets its plane memory to 17 after the block.\n\nThe pin fanuc_post::preamble posts two sections through each post and\nchecks that each preamble has G17 and G94 before the first motion.\n77 recorded programs move by the preamble line only. The dialect\ndiversity test now separates Fanuc and Doosan DNM on a braked rotary\nindex, because on the drill stream the missing G17 was their only\ndifference.\n\nFixes #4346\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
